From: Son Luong Ngoc <26684313+sluongng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:37:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fuser: detach busy Linux mounts on unmount

Stopping a session after an unsuccessful unmount can leave a dead
mount attached when Linux reports EBUSY, including for root callers.

Route that result through the existing helper and lazy-detach fallback,
as permission failures already do. Keep non-Linux behavior unchanged.
---
 src/mnt/fuse_pure.rs | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mnt/fuse_pure.rs b/src/mnt/fuse_pure.rs
index 2e0916e153acaad8cb2eeb38fd826f80f86bb586..0ecb9cfbf67f0fdd2ff446e4cea2b7d232daa411 100644
--- a/src/mnt/fuse_pure.rs
+++ b/src/mnt/fuse_pure.rs
@@ -64,9 +64,12 @@ impl Drop for Mount {
             return;
         }
         if let Err(err) = super::libc_umount(&self.mountpoint) {
-            if err.kind() == PermissionDenied {
-                // Linux always returns EPERM for non-root users.  We have to let the
-                // library go through the setuid-root "fusermount -u" to unmount.
+            if err.kind() == PermissionDenied
+                || (cfg!(target_os = "linux") && err.raw_os_error() == Some(libc::EBUSY))
+            {
+                // Non-root Linux callers need the setuid helper. A busy Linux mount
+                // also needs the existing lazy-detach path, even when owned by root;
+                // otherwise stopping the session can leave a dead attached mount.
                 fuse_unmount_pure(&self.mountpoint)
             } else {
                 error!("Unmount failed: {}", err)
